-- THE CR1 CRYO SHEET REPAIR OF 2026-10-17 (canon 0.30.512). The owner, 2026-10-17: the floor's cryo sheet is the truth,
-- and the historical and current state in the app must match it for cryo entries. Compared against the pre_cr1 snapshot
-- (2026-10-17 20:02 UTC). Every package the app holds is on the sheet; the sheet holds more. This file:
--   1. Restores the 15 outputs of 26016 voided on 2026-09-26 when its first run was unfinished, onto 26016's live run,
--      with their 15 ledger items. All 15 stand in METRC.
--   2. Sets three categories to what the sheet and METRC both say (tags ending 1207 and 1262 to BUD, 1717 to WPR).
--   3. Schedules a run for 26065 and for 26068 (the floor ran both; the app had no run) on their free trim containers,
--      the way the Schedule button does.
--   4. Adds the outputs the app is missing, each on its lot's run, under the sheet's tag, category and weight, with the
--      sheet's day as the cryo date. On a finished run the output is dated just before the finish, so it reads as a
--      regular output and no Shake file pends.
-- Left out by the owner's word: the six 2026-09-15 and 16 rows from indoor lots never in the app, and the one row
-- with no source. Held for the floor: the seven 26066 rows (that lot was trimmed outside the app, so it has no
-- containers to run). The app keeps its own weight where the sheet differs by a few grams.
--
-- Every statement is guarded; a second run changes nothing. Statements that find their lot already scheduled or a tag
-- already entered by the floor skip that row. Rehearsed twice on a copy of the snapshot.
-- Take a snapshot from the main folder's app/, then run it from the main folder's app/:
--   node scripts/db-snapshot.mjs pre_cr1_apply
--   node scripts/repair-apply.mjs scripts/repairs/2026-10-17_cr1_cryo_sheet.sql

